WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.027
Why an engineer needs this lesson.

2
00:00:02.307 --> 00:00:12.333
Regulation is usually someone else’s job until a launch is blocked or a customer’s procurement questionnaire asks what you have done about the EU AI Act.

3
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:25.285
This lesson gives you enough to have that conversation well: the dates, who is responsible for what, and which artifacts an engineering team should produce so that legal and compliance colleagues have something to work with.

4
00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:26.589
Two cautions.

5
00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:36.768
First, this is not legal advice, and the details move: the EU amended its law in 2026 and US policy shifted twice in two years.

6
00:00:37.048 --> 00:00:44.941
Every date below was checked on 11 November 2026 against the cited text; check again before relying on it.

7
00:00:45.221 --> 00:00:52.432
Second, the frontier-model rules that get headlines mostly bind the handful of companies that train the largest models.

8
00:00:52.712 --> 00:01:01.907
What binds most teams is less dramatic: transparency duties, risk classification of specific use cases, data protection, and sector law.

9
00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:04.597
Knowing which is which saves a lot of anxiety.
